{"_id":"68a736358ec3d8323af1db01","nodeId":"JAgjrf5WDXiorZ6gFRzTc","roadmapSlug":"rust","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:32.844Z","description":"# Hashmap\n\n`HashMap<K, V>` stores key-value pairs using hashing for fast lookups, insertions, and removals. Keys must be unique; duplicate keys replace old values. Rust uses cryptographically strong hashing for security. Items are unordered. Example: `HashMap::new()` or `HashMap::from([(\"key\", \"value\")])`.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"HashMap in std::collections","url":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/collections/struct.HashMap.html","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfdd29"},{"type":"official","title":"Storing Keys With Associated Values In Hash Maps","url":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/ch08-03-hash-maps.html?highlight=hashmap#storing-keys-with-associated-values-in-hash-maps","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfdd2a"},{"type":"article","title":"Hash Table","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hash_table","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfdd2b"},{"type":"video","title":"HashMaps: key-value stores in Rust","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BfmSYuDdg8Q","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfdd2c"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:07:02.070Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/rust/content/JAgjrf5WDXiorZ6gFRzTc.md"}